{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Show me, I pray, Your glory.</b> And although they of blessed memory said (Mekhilta on Exodus 15:2) that Israel saw Him at the shore of the sea, and it is written (Exodus 33:11) ״וְדִבֶּר ה׳ אֶל מֹשֶׁה פָּנִים אֶל פָּנִים״ — this is nothing but a vision of consuming fire. And although HaShem said to Aaron and Miriam (Numbers 12:7) ״לֹא כֵן עַבְדִּי מֹשֶׁה וְגוֹ׳ וּמַרְאֶה וְגוֹ׳ וּתְמוּנַת ה׳ יַבִּיט״ — this is nothing but a likeness of supernal light. And Moses wanted to have recognition of Him, blessed be He, a particular knowledge, so that his intellect could grasp an aspect of the divinity, for he saw that the hour was propitious and opened his mouth to ask."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:28.888423806Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}